---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl } from '../lib/site';
const faqs = [
  ['How do I download a YouTube thumbnail?', 'Copy the video link from YouTube, paste it into the field above, and select Get thumbnails. Choose an available size, then select Download JPG. You will get the original image at the displayed resolution, with no resizing or added watermark.'],
  ['Can I download HD YouTube thumbnails?', 'Yes, when the video has a high-resolution thumbnail. The largest common version is 1280 × 720 pixels, but availability varies by video. This tool checks the available images and selects the largest one it finds. It does not upscale a smaller image.'],
  ['Does this work with YouTube Shorts?', 'Yes. Paste a youtube.com/shorts/ link just like a regular video link. We retrieve the thumbnail images YouTube makes available for that video. Their shape and crop may differ from the vertical preview shown in the Shorts feed.'],
  ['Why is the highest-resolution image missing?', 'Some videos, especially older uploads, do not have every thumbnail size. We show only the versions that load successfully. If Max resolution is missing, choose the largest available option instead.'],
  ['How do I save a thumbnail on my phone?', 'Tap Download JPG and follow your browser’s download prompt. If your browser opens the image instead, use its save or share option. You can also select Open image, then touch and hold the picture to save it. The exact steps depend on your browser.'],
  ['What links can I use?', 'You can use standard YouTube watch links, youtu.be short links, Shorts, live video links, and embedded video links. A video ID works too. Links to channels or playlists without a specific video are not supported.'],
  ['Are my links saved?', 'This tool does not save your search history. Your browser reads the video ID locally and requests images directly from YouTube’s image servers. Those requests share ordinary connection information with YouTube. See our Privacy page for details.'],
  ['Can I reuse the thumbnails I download?', 'Downloading an image does not transfer the rights to it. For reuse, make sure you own the image, have permission, or have another valid basis for using it. This tool is independent of YouTube and the video creators.'],
];
const schema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'YT Thumbnail Downloader', url: absoluteUrl('/'), applicationCategory: 'MultimediaApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', browserRequirements: 'Requires JavaScript and a modern web browser.', description: 'Preview and download available YouTube video thumbnails as original JPG images in your browser.', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' } };
---
<Layout title="YT Thumbnail Downloader – Download YouTube Thumbnails" description="Download YouTube thumbnails in the highest available quality. Paste a video or Shorts link, preview the available sizes, and save the original JPG. Free, no sign-up.">
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <p class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> A free tool for creators &amp; the curious</p>
    <h1 id="page-title">YT Thumbnail Downloader<span class="brand-dot">.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-subtitle">Get the thumbnail behind any YouTube video.</p>
    <p class="hero-description">Paste a link. Pick your size. Save the original image.<br class="desktop-break" /> No account, no installs, no extra steps.</p>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-heading"><span class="tool-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="14" rx="3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="m10 8 5 3-5 3V8Z" fill="currentColor"/><path d="M8 21h8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><div><h2>Your next thumbnail starts here</h2><p>A YouTube video, Short, or live video link.</p></div></div>
      <form id="downloader-form" novalidate>
        <label for="video-url">YouTube video link</label>
        <div class="input-row"><div class="url-input-wrap"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m10 13 4-4m-6 7-1 1a4 4 0 0 1-6-6l4-4a4 4 0 0 1 6 0m2 1 1-1a4 4 0 0 1 6 6l-4 4a4 4 0 0 1-6 0" transform="translate(1 0)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><input id="video-url" name="video" type="text" inputmode="url" placeholder="Paste a YouTube link or video ID" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="url-error input-help" /></div><button class="button button-primary" id="get-thumbnails" type="submit">Get thumbnails <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div>
        <p id="url-error" class="field-error" hidden></p>
        <div class="input-footer"><p id="input-help">Supports youtube.com &amp; youtu.be links</p><button id="try-example" class="text-button" type="button">Try an example <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div>
      </form>
      <p id="downloader-status" class="tool-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <noscript><p class="notice">Enable JavaScript to find and download thumbnails. The guides below are available without it.</p></noscript>
    </div>
    <div class="trust-row"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 10 3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Original JPG files</span><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 10 3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Highest available quality</span><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 10 3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Works in your browser</span></div>
  </section>

  <section id="thumbnail-results" class="results container" hidden aria-labelledby="results-title">
    <div class="section-topline"><div><p class="eyebrow">Ready for a closer look</p><h2 id="results-title">Your thumbnail<span class="brand-dot">.</span></h2></div><button id="clear-thumbnail" class="text-button" type="button">Clear result <span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button></div>
    <div class="result-grid"><div class="preview-surface"><img id="thumbnail-preview" alt="YouTube video thumbnail preview" /></div><div class="result-controls"><div class="result-current"><span class="eyebrow" id="thumbnail-quality"></span><p id="thumbnail-dimensions"></p><span class="file-type">JPG · Original image</span></div><div class="quality-heading">Choose a size</div><div id="quality-options" role="group" aria-label="Available thumbnail sizes"></div><a id="download-thumbnail" class="button button-primary" href="#">Download JPG <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><div class="result-actions"><a id="open-thumbnail" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open image ↗</a><button id="copy-thumbnail-link" class="text-button" type="button">Copy image link</button></div><p class="save-hint">On mobile, you can also open the image and touch and hold to save it.</p><div id="copy-link-fallback" hidden><label for="thumbnail-link">Copy this image link</label><input id="thumbnail-link" type="text" readonly /></div></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-section container section-space" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">From link to image</p><h2 id="how-title">Three steps. One great thumbnail.</h2><p>Keep a copy of your own artwork, collect a reference with permission, or take a closer look at the details.</p></div>
    <ol class="steps"><li><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Copy the video link</h3><p>Open a YouTube video or Short and copy its link from the address bar or Share menu.</p></li><li><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Find your thumbnail</h3><p>Paste the link above. We check the available images and show the largest version first.</p></li><li><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Pick a size &amp; save</h3><p>Preview the available sizes, then download the original JPG straight to your device.</p></li></ol>
  </section>

  <section class="sizes-section container section-space" aria-labelledby="sizes-title">
    <div class="sizes-panel"><div class="sizes-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A little clarity on quality</p><h2 id="sizes-title">The right size.<br />The original pixels.</h2><p>YouTube makes thumbnails available in several sizes. We find what exists and keep the image exactly as it is.</p><div class="size-illustration" aria-hidden="true"><div class="frame-large"><span>1280 × 720</span><div class="frame-small"><span>320 × 180</span></div></div></div></div><div class="sizes-table-wrap"><table class="sizes-table"><caption>Common YouTube thumbnail sizes</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Quality</th><th scope="col">Typical size</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Max resolution <span class="tag">HD</span></th><td>1280 × 720</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Standard</th><td>640 × 480</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">High quality</th><td>480 × 360</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Medium</th><td>320 × 180</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="table-note"><span aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span> Not every video has every size. Your results show the actual dimensions, with the highest available quality selected.</p><p class="size-footnote">No upscaling. No cropping. No added watermarks.</p></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section container section-space" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="faq-title">A few common questions.</h2><p>A little help with links, image quality, and saving your thumbnails.</p></div><div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(([question, answer]) => <details><summary>{question}<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>{answer}{question === 'Are my links saved?' && <> <a href="/privacy/">Read our privacy policy.</a></>}</p></details>)}</div></section>
  <div class="closing-note container"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Small tool. Original images. Always free to use.</div>
</Layout>
<script>
  import '../scripts/downloader';
</script>
